From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:16:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] A drain looks at its pipeline in one walk, making nothing

Every drain of every connection checked that the server's own handlers sit
together with nothing outbound behind them before framing packets itself: a
list of every handler's name, then a lookup by name for each of five. In a
live match over the network (VPS-B, 104 players) that was 4% of the event
loop. The contexts are now walked once, by their links, under the pipeline's
lock as names() takes it; a pipeline of another kind is checked as before.
Tests put a plugin's handler among the server's own and take it out again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/AthenaPipelineWalk.java b/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/AthenaPipelineWalk.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3983b9b611901cc90a909cb3bb19a80771cf023f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/AthenaPipelineWalk.java
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+package io.netty.channel;
+
+/**
+ * Athena - walks a pipeline's contexts in order without making anything. {@link ChannelPipeline#names()}
+ * makes a list of every name, and each {@code get(name)} after it walks the pipeline again; the server
+ * looks at its own handlers this way once for every connection's drain, some two thousand times a
+ * second with a hundred players. The links between contexts are the package's own, hence this class
+ * here. Walk under {@code synchronized (pipeline)}, as names() does; the server's jar keeps Netty in
+ * the same package and class loader (it is not relocated).
+ */
+public final class AthenaPipelineWalk {
+
+    private AthenaPipelineWalk() {
+    }
+
+    /** Whether {@code pipeline} can be walked here; a pipeline of another kind cannot. */
+    public static boolean walkable(ChannelPipeline pipeline) {
+        return pipeline instanceof DefaultChannelPipeline;
+    }
+
+    /** The first handler's context, or {@link #end} if there are none. */
+    public static ChannelHandlerContext first(ChannelPipeline pipeline) {
+        return ((DefaultChannelPipeline) pipeline).head.next;
+    }
+
+    /** The context after the last handler's: the walk is over when it gets here. */
+    public static ChannelHandlerContext end(ChannelPipeline pipeline) {
+        return ((DefaultChannelPipeline) pipeline).tail;
+    }
+
+    public static ChannelHandlerContext next(ChannelHandlerContext context) {
+        return ((AbstractChannelHandlerContext) context).next;
+    }
+}
